Interview Answer (Senior Level)

"The tray icon is not drawn by Python itself. My application uses the pystray library as a bridge between Python and the Windows Shell API. First, Pillow loads the .ico file into memory as an image object. Then pystray.Icon creates an internal representation of the tray icon and its context menu. When run_detached() is called, pystray starts a dedicated tray message loop on a background thread and registers the icon with the Windows Shell (Explorer.exe). Explorer is responsible for rendering the icon in the notification area and forwarding user interactions—such as clicks and menu selections—back to the registered callback functions in my Python application. This separation keeps the GUI responsive while allowing the tray icon to behave like a native Windows application."
